\ A 4-in-1 MAX7219 matrix on SPI3 (PC10 CLK, PC12 DIN, PC9 CS), 16-bit  ok.
\ frames: the first word sent goes to the chip farthest from DIN. At power  ok.
\ on the digit registers hold noise, which shows once shutdown is off.  ok.
#!attach 1 matrix PC9 PC10 PC12 chips=4
$48000800 constant GPIOC  ok.
$40003C00 constant SPI3  ok.
: pins ( -- )  ok.
  %100 $4002104C bis!  1 15 lshift $40021058 bis!         \ GPIOC, SPI3  ok.
  1 9 lshift GPIOC $18 + !                                \ CS high  ok.
  %11 18 lshift GPIOC bic!  %01 18 lshift GPIOC bis!      \ PC9 output  ok.
  %11 20 lshift %11 24 lshift or GPIOC bic!  %10 20 lshift %10 24 lshift or GPIOC bis!  ok.
  $F 8 lshift $F 16 lshift or GPIOC $24 + bic!  6 8 lshift 6 16 lshift or GPIOC $24 + bis! ;  \ AF6  ok.
: spi-on ( -- ) $0F00 SPI3 4 + !  $354 SPI3 ! ;            \ 16-bit frames, master, /8  ok.
: >16 ( u -- ) begin SPI3 8 + @ 2 and until  SPI3 $C + h!  begin SPI3 8 + @ $80 and 0= until ;  ok.
: cs-lo 1 9 lshift 16 lshift GPIOC $18 + ! ;  ok.
: cs-hi 1 9 lshift GPIOC $18 + ! ;  ok.
: all ( reg v -- ) swap 8 lshift or  cs-lo 4 0 do dup >16 loop drop cs-hi ;  ok.
pins spi-on  ok.
#!matrix 1
................................
................................
................................
................................
................................
................................
................................
................................
Bus	CS PC9 · CLK PC10 · DIN PC12
Chain	4 × MAX7219 · 32 × 8 LEDs
Mode	shutdown (C = 0): dark
Intensity	0 · 1/32
Scan limit	0 · rows 0–0 only
Decode	none: each bit an LED
Chips	all set alike
$C 1 all  $B 7 all  $A 3 all  9 0 all  ok.

[chip] MAX7219: the module runs from 5 V and wants at least 3.5 V for a high on DIN, CLK and CS; a 3.3 V pin is below that. It mostly works on the bench; a level shifter makes it sure
